        setup: {
          players: '2-8 players. Individual play or 2-player partnerships.',
          deck: '105 cards (2 x 52 + 1 Joker). All 2s and the Joker are wild.',
          equipment: 'Two standard decks, score sheet.',
          dealing: 'Each player is dealt 13 cards. The remainder forms the stock pile. The top card is flipped to start the discard pile.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Score the most points over seven hands by fulfilling each hand's specific meld contract and eventually 'going rummy' (discarding all cards).",
          gameplay: "1. **Draw**: Draw the top card of the stock or the discard pile. 2. **Stealing Wilds**: If an opponent has a meld on the table containing a wild card (2 or Joker), and you hold the 'natural' card that wild is representing, you may swap your natural card for that wild and add the wild to your hand. 3. **Melding**: Lay down the specific contract for the current hand. You cannot lay down any other melds until your contract is complete. 4. **Offering**: At the end of your turn, you MUST offer one card from your hand to the table. Starting from your left, each player has a chance to take it and discard a card from their hand to maintain count. 5. **Going Rummy**: To end the hand, you must meld your entire hand and have one card left to discard.",
          keyRules: [
            'Contract Progression: Hand 1 (Two sets of 3); Hand 7 (Three runs of 4). Requirements increase each hand.',
            "Aces & Wilds Offerting: Aces and Wild cards can ONLY be offered to the player on your immediate left. If they don't want it, it goes to the discard pile.",
            'Discard Pile Capture: You can only take the top discard if you use it in a meld immediately.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize high-value cards (Jokers) in your melds. If you lose the hand, having a Joker in your hand is a 50-point penalty.',
          intermediate: "The Offering Phase: Offer cards that are 'dead' to the board (e.g., a card whose duplicates have already been melded or discarded). Never offer a card that helps an opponent complete a run.",
          advanced: "Wild Hijacking: Keep 'natural' cards that match current wild positions in opponents' melds. Steal the wild only when you are ready to complete your own contract or go rummy.",
          tips: [
            'Wait to lay down your contract until you have almost your whole hand filled. Once you lay down, opponents can steal your wilds!',
            'Hand 7 (Three runs of 4) is the decider; the winning bonus for that hand is usually enough to overcome any early lead.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
